<title>PORTUGAL: Proholding management launches buyout.</title>
<headline>Proholding management launches buyout.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Management at chemicals group Proholding has launched a buyout offer at 4,255 escudos per share, according to a statement sent to Portugal's Financial Markets Committee.</p>
<p>The statement, a copy of which was sent to Reuters, said that the management had already reached an accord with major shareholders for the purchase of 1.39 million shares, equal to 87 percent of the company's capital.</p>
<p>Proholding is controlled by the family of Belmiro de Azevedo, president of the Sonae group.</p>
<p>The company's stock was suspended on Wednesday at 4,750 escudos.</p>
<p>(( --Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035 ))</p>
